{"node_id": "real_073_Adaptation-in-a-heterogeneous-environment-II_13_HY_014", "node_type": "evidence", "status": "HYBRID_SHADOW_CANDIDATE", "unit_type": "TEXT", "source_atom_ids": ["D0015"], "source_fragment_ids": ["D0015_F001"], "source_visual_bundle_ids": [], "plain_text": "More precisely, $\\lambda_3(\\mathbf{O}_1,\\mathbf{O}_2,\\mathcal{O})\\rightarrow \\lambda_1+\\delta$ while $\\lambda_3(\\mathbf{O}_1,\\mathbf{O}_2,\\mathbf{O}_1)\\rightarrow \\lambda_1+\\delta/2$ as $\\beta\\rightarrow+\\infty$ .", "semantic_text": "More precisely, $\\lambda_3(\\mathbf{O}_1,\\mathbf{O}_2,\\mathcal{O})\\rightarrow \\lambda_1+\\delta$ while $\\lambda_3(\\mathbf{O}_1,\\mathbf{O}_2,\\mathbf{O}_1)\\rightarrow \\lambda_1+\\delta/2$ as $\\beta\\rightarrow+\\infty$ .", "visual_description": null, "geometry_members": [{"member_id": "D0015_geometry", "bbox": [160, 1277, 947, 1304], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0015"}], "native_visual_components": [], "production_modified": false, "visual_description_status": "UNVERIFIED_RETRIEVAL_HINT", "node_policy": "bounded-v2", "scoring_mode": "embedding_geometry", "hybrid_model_decision_file": "/hkfs/home/project/hk-project-p0025545/dv3352/Project/remote_runs/node-first-realpdf-20261118/output/nodes_prepared_incremental_non_nasa_after_all_parse_20261119/batch_100/hybrid/real_073_Adaptation-in-a-heterogeneous-environment-II/page_0013/decisions.json"}
{"node_id": "real_073_Adaptation-in-a-heterogeneous-environment-II_13_HY_015", "node_type": "evidence", "status": "HYBRID_SHADOW_CANDIDATE", "unit_type": "TEXT", "source_atom_ids": ["D0016"], "source_fragment_ids": ["D0016_F001"], "source_visual_bundle_ids": [], "plain_text": "We point out that, since $\\lambda_3({\\mathbf{O}}_1,{\\mathbf{O}}_2,{\\mathbf{O}}_1) = \\lambda_3({\\mathbf{O}}_1,{\\mathbf{O}}_1,{\\mathbf{O}}_2)$ by symmetry, the limit\n$\\lambda_1 + \\delta/2 = \\lim_{\\beta\\to+\\infty}\\lambda_3({\\mathbf{O}}_1,{\\mathbf{O}}_2,{\\mathbf{O}}_1) = \\lim_{\\beta\\to+\\infty}\\lambda_3({\\mathbf{O}}_1,{\\mathbf{O}}_1,{\\mathbf{O}}_2)$ is coherent with the limit\n$\\lim_{\\beta\\to+\\infty}\\lambda_3({\\mathbf{O}}_1,{\\mathbf{O}}_1,{\\mathbf{O}}_2) = \\widetilde{\\lambda}_2({\\mathbf{O}}_1,{\\mathbf{O}}_1) = \\lambda_1 + \\delta/2$ , with $\\widetilde{\\lambda}_2({\\mathbf{O}}_1,{\\mathbf{O}}_1)$ being the principal\neigenvalue of (26) in the case of identical optima (see the proof of Proposition 4.7 in\nSection 6.3 for further details).", "semantic_text": "We point out that, since $\\lambda_3({\\mathbf{O}}_1,{\\mathbf{O}}_2,{\\mathbf{O}}_1) = \\lambda_3({\\mathbf{O}}_1,{\\mathbf{O}}_1,{\\mathbf{O}}_2)$ by symmetry, the limit $\\lambda_1 + \\delta/2 = \\lim_{\\beta\\to+\\infty}\\lambda_3({\\mathbf{O}}_1,{\\mathbf{O}}_2,{\\mathbf{O}}_1) = \\lim_{\\beta\\to+\\infty}\\lambda_3({\\mathbf{O}}_1,{\\mathbf{O}}_1,{\\mathbf{O}}_2)$ is coherent with the limit $\\lim_{\\beta\\to+\\infty}\\lambda_3({\\mathbf{O}}_1,{\\mathbf{O}}_1,{\\mathbf{O}}_2) = \\widetilde{\\lambda}_2({\\mathbf{O}}_1,{\\mathbf{O}}_1) = \\lambda_1 + \\delta/2$ , with $\\widetilde{\\lambda}_2({\\mathbf{O}}_1,{\\mathbf{O}}_1)$ being the principal eigenvalue of (26) in the case of identical optima (see the proof of Proposition 4.7 in Section 6.3 for further details).", "visual_description": null, "geometry_members": [{"member_id": "D0016_geometry", "bbox": [157, 1312, 973, 1445], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0016"}], "native_visual_components": [], "production_modified": false, "visual_description_status": "UNVERIFIED_RETRIEVAL_HINT", "node_policy": "bounded-v2", "scoring_mode": "embedding_geometry", "hybrid_model_decision_file": "/hkfs/home/project/hk-project-p0025545/dv3352/Project/remote_runs/node-first-realpdf-20261118/output/nodes_prepared_incremental_non_nasa_after_all_parse_20261119/batch_100/hybrid/real_073_Adaptation-in-a-heterogeneous-environment-II/page_0013/decisions.json"}
